# erhai (OnePlus Pad 3): re-arm the ADSP OTG session after Type-C detach.
# After a detach the ADSP CC attach detection can stay dead until the session
# is re-armed (see /usr/local/sbin/erhai-otg-rearm.sh) -- replugs stay invisible.
#
# EDGE GATE (2026-10-21): the original rule started the service on EVERY port0
# "change" uevent, but this line emits a PHANTOM change every ~4.03 s with no
# partner/role information in the payload, so the service ran ~15x/min and the
# mechanism was disabled on 2026-09-14.  `PROGRAM=... check` is a cheap edge
# detector run inside udev (no service spawn); RESULT=="edge" only matches when a
# partner was seen and then disappeared -- i.e. a REAL detach.
# NOTE: ACTION=="remove" + SYSTEMD_WANTS never fires (systemd drops the start
# request for an already-deleted device) - do not rely on remove rules.
ACTION=="change", SUBSYSTEM=="typec", KERNEL=="port0", \
  PROGRAM="/usr/local/sbin/erhai-otg-rearm.sh check", RESULT=="edge", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}="erhai-otg-rearm.service"
